# .cursorrules for Hammerspoon config
project: Hammerspoon macOS Automation
language: Lua
editor: Cursor
context:
  - Entry point is init.lua, modules live in /modules
  - hs.* is the Hammerspoon global API namespace
  - Do not use require() with .lua extension
  - LuaJIT runtime
style:
  - Keep each module focused on one responsibility
  - Always include error handling in hs.http calls
  - Use hs.logger for persistent logs
integrations:
  - n8n webhooks via hs.http.asyncGet/asyncPost
  - AppleScript via hs.osascript.applescript()
  - Keyboard Maestro via hs.urlevent.openURL()
  - macOS notifications via hs.notify (async feedback without blocking)
  - MQTT / IoT via hs.mqtt (smart home, sensors)
  - WebSockets via hs.websocket (live dashboards, chat bots)
  - Network discovery via hs.network, hs.host
  - Calendar / Reminders via AppleScript or Shortcuts (scheduling hooks)
